# SiteBoy — Cursor Rules (Backend)

## Scope
- Target: backend/CI + server-side reasoning for JS/CSS/JSON in this repo.
- Assume Node 20+, no browser globals unless noted.

## File Ownership (SSoT)
Only these files may own the concern. Others must not implement it.
- Layout math → assets/js/core/mathematical-foundation.js
- Base OO system → assets/js/core/base-component.js
- **Animation logic → assets/js/core/animation-foundation.js**
- Routing/nav → assets/js/core/router.js
- App bootstrap/init → assets/js/core/app.js
- UI components → assets/js/shared/component-library.js
- Specialised widgets (graphs/canvas) → assets/js/shared/specialized-components.js
- Sections/page composition → assets/js/sections/*.js
- All styling → modular CSS system (entry: assets/css/index.css):
  - Palette/reset/typography → assets/css/base.css
  - UI component classes → assets/css/components.css
  - Page structure → assets/css/layout.css
  - Tool interfaces → assets/css/tools.css
  - Utilities & debug → assets/css/utilities.css
  - ⚠ assets/css/styles.css is DEAD (legacy monolith, do NOT edit)
- **Generator UI structure (tab layout for all 22 generators) → assets/js/tools/generators/core/parameter-builder.js**
- **Generator schema + validation → assets/js/tools/generators/core/script-types.js**
- **Modulation engine (driver→shape→range→combine pipeline) → assets/js/tools/generators/core/modulation-engine.js**
- **Driver registry (lfo/linear/expression/etc.) → assets/js/tools/generators/core/driver-registry.js**
- **Expression context (cheat-sheet variables/helpers) → assets/js/tools/generators/core/expression-context.js**
- **Project tracker (roadmap / TODO list) → blog/docs/todo/** — the only authoritative roadmap.

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## TODO SYSTEM (PROJECT TRACKING) — MANDATORY
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The folder `blog/docs/todo/` is the single source of truth for in-flight, planned, and out-of-scope work. Other "next-steps" / "todo" / "plan" docs (e.g. `blog/docs/temp/*-next-steps.md`, `*-todo.md`, `*-plan.md`) are tool-internal feeders only; they are not authoritative.

### Layout
- `blog/docs/todo/index.md` — dashboard. One table per area (A–H). One row per item with current status.
- `blog/docs/todo/<ID>-<slug>.md` — one file per item. Owns its status, sub-tasks, blockers, notes.
- `blog/docs/todo/out-of-scope.md` — explicit non-goals.

### Defined terms (closed sets)
- **Status**: `TODO` | `WIP` | `BLOCKED` | `REVIEW` | `DONE`.
- **Priority**: `P0` (critical path) | `P1` (must ship next release) | `P2` (deferrable one release) | `P3` (no deadline).
- **ID format**: `<Area>.<n>`. Areas are letters A–H. IDs are permanent.

### Required behaviour (every agent + every contributor)

1. **Read before coding.** Before any non-trivial change, read `blog/docs/todo/index.md`. Locate the item ID that covers your work.
2. **Append if missing.** If no item exists, append one to the correct area in `index.md` and create `<ID>-<slug>.md` using the template established in existing files (`Status`, `Priority`, `Owner file(s)`, `Blockers`, `Blocks`, `Last touched`, `Goal`, `Done when`, `Sub-tasks`, `Notes`, `References`).
3. **Status flips happen in two places.** Edit the item file's header `Status:` line **and** the matching row in `index.md`. Both must agree at all times.
4. **`Done when` is a single, verifiable predicate.** Vague verbs (`polish`, `improve`, `clean up`) are forbidden. Acceptance is binary.
5. **IDs are permanent.** Status flips. The ID does not. Renumbering breaks history.
6. **Blockers are explicit item IDs.** "Blocked by complexity" is not a blocker.
7. **DONE only after the predicate is verified.** Not "implementation landed". Verified.
8. **WIP has a 14-day SLA.** A row with `WIP` for >14 days must advance to `REVIEW` or be re-scoped.

### When user asks for new work
- If the request maps to an existing item, mention the ID and proceed.
- If not, propose an ID and add the row before starting code.

### Out of scope
- Anything listed in `blog/docs/todo/out-of-scope.md` requires an ADR to move back into scope. Do not silently re-introduce.

### Ideas and projects (see `blog/docs/todo/index.md` § Ideas folder)
- If the same concept exists under `blog/ideas/art/generative/` and `blog/ideas/tools/`, **generative is canonical** for linking and duplicate marking; `tools/` is a feeder unless it is the only copy.
- Portfolio entries (`#projects/<slug>`) **need not** map to a shipped tool; idea-only project pages are valid (B1).

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## ABSOLUTE PROHIBITIONS — STOP AND CHECK BEFORE WRITING CODE
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### DOM Manipulation — FORBIDDEN outside BaseComponent/ComponentLibrary
BEFORE writing any code that creates DOM elements, STOP and ask:
- Am I in BaseComponent, ComponentLibrary, foundation.js, or layout.js?
- If NO → VIOLATION. Use ComponentLibrary components instead.

**FORBIDDEN PATTERNS IN TOOL/SECTION FILES:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER WRITE THESE IN TOOL FILES:
document.createElement()
.innerHTML =
.appendChild()
.insertBefore()
.removeChild()
```

**INSTEAD:**
```javascript
// ✅ Use existing ComponentLibrary components
// ✅ Or extend ComponentLibrary with new components FIRST
```

### Colors — ONLY VGA Palette Variables
BEFORE writing any color value, STOP and ask:
- Is this var(--vga-*) or var(--c-*)?
- If NO → VIOLATION

**FORBIDDEN:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER:
'#ff5500'           // Any non-VGA hex
'rgb(255,100,0)'    // Any rgb()
'rgba()'            // Any rgba()
'hsl()'             // Any hsl()
'red', 'blue'       // Named colors
```

**ALLOWED:**
```javascript
// ✅ ONLY these exact VGA colors in canvas:
'#000000', '#800000', '#008000', '#808000',
'#000080', '#800080', '#008080', '#c0c0c0',
'#808080', '#ff0000', '#00ff00', '#ffff00',
'#0000ff', '#ff00ff', '#00ffff', '#ffffff'

// ✅ In CSS/styles: var(--vga-*) or var(--c-*)
```

### Sizing — ONLY F-Based Calculations
BEFORE writing any dimension, STOP and ask:
- Is this using var(--f) or calc(var(--f) * N)?
- If NO → VIOLATION

**FORBIDDEN IN JS:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER in inline styles:
'padding: 8px'      // Use calc(var(--f) * 0.57)
'font-size: 11px'   // Use calc(var(--f) * 0.79)
'width: 200px'      // Use CSS classes or F-based calc
```

### Inline Styles — FORBIDDEN in Tool/Section Files
**FORBIDDEN:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER:
element.style.cssText = '...'
element.style.property = '...'
```

**INSTEAD:**
- Define CSS classes in the appropriate module (components.css / tools.css / layout.css / utilities.css)
- Apply classes: `element.className = 'my-class'`
- Use CSS variables for dynamic values

### CSS File Routing — NEVER Edit styles.css
`assets/css/styles.css` is a dead legacy monolith. The live system is modular.
BEFORE writing any CSS, STOP and route to the correct file:
- Palette vars / reset / typography → `assets/css/base.css`
- UI component classes (buttons, dropdowns, gallery items) → `assets/css/components.css`
- Page structure (containers, grids, responsive) → `assets/css/layout.css`
- Tool interfaces (ToolBase, sidebar, canvas) → `assets/css/tools.css`
- Utilities, debug, scrollbar → `assets/css/utilities.css`

**FORBIDDEN:**
```
// ❌ NEVER:
editing assets/css/styles.css (dead file)
creating new .css files (use existing modules)
```

### Animation APIs — ONLY AnimationFoundation
**FORBIDDEN:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER in tool files:
requestAnimationFrame()
cancelAnimationFrame()
setInterval() // for animations
setTimeout()  // for animations
```

**REQUIRED:**
```javascript
// ✅ ALWAYS:
new AnimationFoundation.AnimationLoop({ onFrame: fn })
new AnimationFoundation.IntervalAnimator({ interval: ms, onTick: fn })
```

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Mandatory Patterns
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- All UI classes extend `BaseComponent`.
- Instances: `const x = new X(...); this.componentInstances.push(x)`.
- All dimensional math via `MathematicalFoundation.calculateDimensions(kind|props)`.
- All animations via `AnimationFoundation` classes.
- No manual DOM outside BaseComponent internals.
- No manual RAF/setInterval for animations.

## Style Constraints (VGA/Mono)
- Colors: only CSS vars `var(--vga-*)`. No raw hex/rgb/hsl.
- Typeface: Atkinson Hyperlegible only.
- Disallow: gradients, shadows, rounded corners.
- Use math/tokens for dimensions (no ad-hoc px for layout logic).

## Tab Limit
- At most 4 tabs in ToolBase sidebar (ceiling, not target)
- Use the minimum number of tabs that map to genuinely distinct user concerns
- Reaching the cap is a smell — consolidate into blocks within tabs
- NEVER exceed 4 tabs

## Build Chronology (observable path)
app → router → destroy → section → subheader → JSON → blocks → render → URL

## DO / DON'T Examples

### DO:
```javascript
// Extend BaseComponent
class Dropdown extends BaseComponent { ... }

// Track instances
const dd = new Dropdown(o); 
this.componentInstances.push(dd);

// Use MathematicalFoundation
MathematicalFoundation.calculateDimensions('dropdown');

// Use AnimationFoundation
this.animator = new AnimationFoundation.AnimationLoop({ 
    onFrame: () => this.draw() 
});

// Use VGA colors
ctx.fillStyle = '#000000';
```

### DON'T:
```javascript
// ❌ Raw DOM
const el = document.createElement('div');
el.innerHTML = '<span>Bad</span>';

// ❌ Layout math outside Foundation
const w = px * 0.62;

// ❌ Raw animation APIs
this.animationFrame = requestAnimationFrame(...);
this.interval = setInterval(...);

// ❌ Non-VGA colors
ctx.fillStyle = '#ff5500';

// ❌ Inline styles
element.style.padding = '8px';
```

## JSON Page Contract (must hold)
Required keys: header (str), subheader (str), url ("/kebab"), blocks (array of {type, props}).
type ∈ {SectionDropdown, TextBlock, ImageBlock, Grid, Chart, CanvasWidget}.

## Quick Reference
- Build page: JSON → ComponentLibrary only.
- Never break the file-ownership map.
- Enforce mathematical precision for all dimensions.

## Rewrite/Generation Guidance

### Before generating tool code, mentally check:
- [ ] Will this create DOM elements? → Must be in ComponentLibrary
- [ ] Will this set colors? → Must be VGA variables
- [ ] Will this set dimensions? → Must use F-system
- [ ] Will this animate? → Must use AnimationFoundation
- [ ] Will this style elements? → Must use CSS classes

### If a feature needs custom UI:
1. First: Check if ComponentLibrary has it
2. If not: Extend ComponentLibrary with new component
3. Then: Use the component in the tool
4. Never: Create DOM directly in tool file

## Minimal Checks (heuristics you must respect when editing)
Reject/avoid code that introduces:
- document.* / window.* outside BaseComponent
- class BaseComponent outside its owner
- calculateDimensions( outside MathematicalFoundation
- requestAnimationFrame/cancelAnimationFrame/setInterval for animations
- routing (pushState, popstate, location.hash) outside router.js
- bootstrap/initialize outside app.js
- raw colours or border-radius/box-shadow/text-shadow anywhere

Sections must:
- import ComponentLibrary
- load JSON
- render from JSON blocks only

Animations must:
- Use AnimationFoundation classes
- Call animator.destroy() in cleanup
- Never implement custom RAF/setInterval loops

## Output Contract
- Keep diffs minimal; do not add new files that duplicate owned concerns.
- When unsure where logic goes: default to the owner listed above; never inline.

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## LIBRARY PARADIGM DISTINCTION
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Two Code Ecosystems

| Library | Location | Paradigm | OOP Required? |
|---------|----------|----------|---------------|
| **Algorithms Library** | `assets/js/shared/algorithms/` | Functional | NO |
| **Site Components** | `assets/js/shared/`, `assets/js/core/`, `assets/js/tools/` | OOP | YES |
| **Reference Docs** | `blog/ideas/reference documentation/` | N/A (research) | N/A |

### Algorithms Library Rules (PURE FUNCTIONAL CODE)
- Location: `assets/js/shared/algorithms/`
- Pure functions, no side effects, no DOM
- MUST cite source reference documentation
- MUST include `@source`, `@wikipedia`, `@formula` in JSDoc
- CAN use any color values (algorithms, not rendering)
- CAN use any dimensions (abstract math, not layout)

### Site Component Rules (PRODUCTION UI CODE)
- All rules in this document apply (BaseComponent, VGA, F-system, etc.)
- MUST wrap algorithms library functions in OOP components
- MUST NOT duplicate algorithm logic (import from algorithms library)

### When Building a Tool:
1. **Algorithm logic** → Use/extend algorithms library (functional)
   ```javascript
   import { Noise, Patterns, SDF } from '../shared/algorithms/index.js';
   ```
2. **UI/rendering** → Use site components (OOP, BaseComponent, ToolBase)
3. **Never mix** → Don't put algorithms in tool files, don't put DOM in algorithms

### Algorithms Library Source Citation Standard
Every function in `assets/js/shared/algorithms/` MUST include:
```javascript
/**
 * [Description]
 * 
 * @source blog/ideas/reference documentation/[CATEGORY]/[Article].md
 * @wikipedia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/[Article]
 * @section [Section containing formula]
 * @formula [Exact LaTeX from reference doc]
 */
```

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## DEBUG LOGGING SYSTEM
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### NEVER Use console.log Directly
**FORBIDDEN:**
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER:
console.log('Initializing component...');
console.log('Route changed to:', path);
console.log('Layout calculated:', dims);
```

**REQUIRED:**
```javascript
// ✅ ALWAYS use debugLog with category:
window.debugLog('INIT', 'Initializing component...');
window.debugLog('NAVIGATION', 'Route changed to:', path);
window.debugLog('LAYOUT', 'Layout calculated:', dims);
```

### Debug Categories (5 total)

| Category | Purpose | Default | When to Use |
|----------|---------|---------|-------------|
| **INIT** | Initialization/startup | OFF | Component loading, version info, system ready messages |
| **LAYOUT** | Layout calculations | OFF | F-system, dimensions, PageContainer states, resize events |
| **NAVIGATION** | Route/nav changes | OFF | Route changes, subheader updates, navigation setup |
| **TOOLS** | Tool operations | OFF | Tool loading, rendering, tool-specific operations |
| **VERBOSE** | Repetitive operations | OFF | Dropdown open/close, cleanup, cache hits (rarely needed) |

### Category Assignment Rules

**INIT** - Module loading & initialization:
- Component library ready messages
- Section "ready" messages
- Router/app initialization
- System version info
- One-time startup events

**LAYOUT** - Dimension & positioning:
- F-system calculations
- PageContainer layout application
- Margin/frame calculations
- Subheader state changes (show/hide affecting layout)
- Resize recalculations

**NAVIGATION** - Routing & navigation:
- Route changes (hash changes)
- Subheader title updates
- Navigation dropdown setup
- Prev/next navigation
- Section transitions

**TOOLS** - Tool-specific operations:
- Tool loading/rendering
- Tool initialization
- Tool-specific state changes
- Tool operations (not covered by other categories)

**VERBOSE** - High-frequency operations:
- Dropdown open/close (can fire 18+ times per action)
- Section cleanup (happens on every nav)
- JSON cache hits
- Repetitive render confirmations
- Operations that normally don't need logging

### Exception: Keep console.error/warn
```javascript
// ✅ ALWAYS keep these (not debug, actual problems):
console.error('Failed to load:', error);
console.warn('Deprecated API used');
```

### Usage Examples

**Converting existing logs:**
```javascript
// OLD:
console.log('🚀 SiteBoy App initialized');
console.log(`🧭 Route change: ${section}`);
console.log('📐 Layout applied');
console.log('🔄 Dropdown closed');

// NEW:
window.debugLog('INIT', '🚀 SiteBoy App initialized');
window.debugLog('NAVIGATION', `🧭 Route change: ${section}`);
window.debugLog('LAYOUT', '📐 Layout applied');
window.debugLog('VERBOSE', '🔄 Dropdown closed');
```

**User controls (available in browser console):**
```javascript
// Enable specific categories
debugToggle('INIT', true);                    // Show initialization
debugToggle(['NAVIGATION', 'TOOLS'], true);   // Multiple categories
debugToggle('ALL', true);                      // Everything
debugToggle('ALL', false);                     // Disable all

// Object syntax
debugToggle({ INIT: true, LAYOUT: true, VERBOSE: false });
```

### Implementation Checklist

When adding new features:
- [ ] Replace ALL console.log with window.debugLog
- [ ] Assign appropriate category (INIT/LAYOUT/NAVIGATION/TOOLS/VERBOSE)
- [ ] Keep console.error/console.warn unchanged
- [ ] Test that logs only appear when category enabled

### File Locations
- Config & utilities: `assets/js/core/config.js`
- Documentation: `blog/docs/temp/debug-log-analysis.md`

### Benefits
- Clean console by default (production-ready)
- Enable only needed logs during debugging
- No performance impact when disabled
- Categorized debugging (no sifting through noise)
- Easy to find repetitive/spammy logs (VERBOSE)

## Scraped design rule corpus (general knowledge)

SiteBoy guides (`blog/docs/guides/standards/design-law.md`, `component-patterns.md`, etc.) **take precedence** over scraped rules where they conflict.

| Need | Read |
| --- | --- |
| One-off design decision | `blog/docs/guides/ai-routing-map.md` §13 |
| End-to-end workflow (capture, publish, extract) | `blog/docs/guides/ai-routing-map.md` §14 |
| Rule lookup by ID | `blog/docs/standards/rules/INDEX.md` → `standards/rules/<category>/<id>.md` |
| All rules in one category | `blog/docs/standards/<category>.md` |
| Top MUST/MUST_NOT only | `blog/docs/standards/hot-rules.md` |

Read only what the task requires; do not load the full corpus into context.

